  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0047 database is a comprehensive system for managing user accounts, email addresses, and various business-related data. It contains 22 tables that work together to store and manage user information, email addresses, customer data, and subscription details. The database starts with the account_emailaddress table, which stores email addresses associated with users, including a unique identifier, the email address itself, a verification status, and a primary flag to indicate the default email address. Each email address is linked to a user through the user_id foreign key, referencing the users_customuser table. The account_emailconfirmation table stores email confirmation details, including the confirmation key and the associated email address. The auth_group table stores group information, while the auth_group_permissions table links groups to permissions, and the auth_permission table stores permission details. The django_admin_log table tracks administrative actions, including the user who performed the action, the object affected, and the action taken. The django_content_type table stores information about the types of content in the database, and the django_migrations table tracks the history of database migrations. The django_session table stores user session data, and the django_site table stores information about the website. The djstripe_customer table stores customer data from a third-party payment gateway, including customer details, payment information, and subscription status. The djstripe_plan table stores plan information, including pricing details and subscription settings. The djstripe_product table stores product information, and the djstripe_subscription table stores subscription details, including customer and plan information. The pegasus_examples_employee table stores employee data, and the pegasus_examples_payment table stores payment information. The teams_invitation table stores team invitation data, including the invited user, the team, and the invitation status. The teams_membership table stores team membership information, including the user, the team, and the user's role. The teams_team table stores team information, including the team name, slug, and subscription details. The users_customuser table stores user information, including username, email, password, and subscription details. The users_customuser_groups table links users to groups, and the users_customuser_user_permissions table links users to permissions.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThe project aims to develop a Django-powered SaaS (Software as a Service) application template named Pegasus. This template facilitates the rapid development of SaaS applications by providing foundational features and adhering to Django best practices. The application supports user management, team collaboration, and subscription billing.\n\nObjectives\n\n- To provide a robust boilerplate for launching SaaS applications quickly.\n- To streamline development by managing core functionalities such as authentication, team setups, and subscription plans.\n- To ensure scalability and best practice compliance using Django.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Developers: Users who will customize and build upon the Pegasus template to create their SaaS products.\n- End Users: Customers of the SaaS applications developed using Pegasus.\n- Administrators: Developers or appointed personnel responsible for managing users, teams, and subscriptions.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. User Management\n   - Users can register, login, and manage their profiles.\n   - Email addresses can be verified and users can have a primary email.\n\n2. Teams and Collaboration\n   - Users can create and join teams.\n   - Invitations to join teams can be managed, and roles assigned within teams.\n   \n3. Subscription Management\n   - Plans can be created and associated with users or teams.\n   - Subscription billing intervals and usage are configurable.\n\n4. Payment Processing\n   - Integration with Stripe for handling customer payments and billing functionalities.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: The system must efficiently handle multiple concurrent users and team operations.\n- Security: Implement robust security measures for user data, including encryption and secure transaction protocols.\n- Compliance: Adhere to legal and industry standards for data protection and online transactions.\n- Performance: Ensure minimal latency and high availability for user interactions and API responses.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0047.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0047\nCREATE TABLE `account_emailaddress` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `is_verified` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `is_primary` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `account_emailaddress_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users_customuser` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `account_emailconfirmation` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `email_address_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `confirmation_key` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `account_emailconfirmation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`email_address_id`) REFERENCES `account_emailaddress` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `auth_group` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `auth_group_permissions` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `group_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `permission_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `auth_group_permissions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`group_id`) REFERENCES `auth_group` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `auth_group_permissions_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`permission_id`) REFERENCES `auth_permission` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `auth_permission` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `codename` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `django_admin_log` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `action_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content_type_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `object_id` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `object_repr` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `action_flag` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  `change_message` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `django_admin_log_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users_customuser` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `django_admin_log_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`content_type_id`) REFERENCES `django_content_type` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `django_content_type` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `app_label` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `model` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `django_migrations` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `app` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `applied` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `django_session` (\n  `session_key` varchar(40) NOT NULL,\n  `session_data` text NOT NULL,\n  `expire_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`session_key`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `django_site` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `domain` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `djstripe_customer` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `stripeCustomerId` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `subscription_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `djstripe_customer_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users_customuser` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `djstripe_plan` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `stripePlanId` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `amount` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `currency` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `djstripe_product` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `stripeProductId` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `djstripe_subscription` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `plan_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `djstripe_subscription_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `djstripe_customer` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `djstripe_subscription_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`plan_id`) REFERENCES `djstripe_plan` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `pegasus_examples_employee` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `pegasus_examples_payment` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `pegasus_examples_payment_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `pegasus_examples_employee` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `teams_invitation` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `invited_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `teams_invitation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`invited_user_id`) REFERENCES `users_customuser` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `teams_invitation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`team_id`) REFERENCES `teams_team` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `teams_membership` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `teams_membership_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users_customuser` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `teams_membership_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`team_id`) REFERENCES `teams_team` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `teams_team` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `slug` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `users_customuser` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(150) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `users_customuser_groups` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `group_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `users_customuser_groups_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users_customuser` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `users_customuser_groups_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`group_id`) REFERENCES `auth_group` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `users_customuser_user_permissions` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `permission_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `users_customuser_user_permissions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users_customuser` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `users_customuser_user_permissions_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`permission_id`) REFERENCES `auth_permission` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
